#   Two language models predict the next word using the probability distributions 
P=[0.5,0.3,0.2] and Q=[0.4,0.4,0.2]. A developer wants to measure how much the second 
model's distribution differs from the first. 
Write a Python program to calculate the KL divergence and to compare the two probability 
distributions with a grouped bar chart.




import numpy as np

P = np.array([0.5,0.3,0.2])
Q = np.array([0.4,0.4,0.2])
D = np.sum(P*np.log(P/Q))
print("KL Divergence:", D)
